# .trivyignore — Security CVE suppressions
#
# Policy: every entry MUST document (1) the vulnerability, (2) why we cannot take the fix NOW,
# (3) what compensating control is in place, and (4) what unblocks the fix.
#
# Review cadence: revisit each entry when its blocking dependency constraint is lifted.
# Owner: project maintainer. Reference: docs/plan/TRAIL.md § Deferred Work.

# ── Python transitive dependencies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# GHSA-f4xh-w4cj-qxq8 (langsmith arbitrary server-side file read)
#   Package    : langsmith < 0.8.18 (transitive via langchain; locked at 0.8.0)
#   Fix        : langsmith >= 0.8.18
#   Why blocked: langsmith >=0.8.18 requires websockets>=15; sie-sdk pins websockets>=14,<15.
#                Verified 2026-07-27: `uv lock` with langsmith==0.8.18 is unsatisfiable while
#                sie-sdk>=0.6.0 remains a direct dependency. (langchain-core 1.4.x is already
#                locked — the old "core pre-release only" blocker is SUPERSEDED.)
#   Compensating control: TracingMiddleware is not mounted; langsmith is transitive via
#                         langchain text-splitters only — file-read vector not reachable from
#                         user input in this application.
#   Unblocked by: sie-sdk raising websockets to >=15 (or dropping the pin). Meterian parity:
#                 `.meterian` library exclusion on langsmith 0.8.0.
GHSA-f4xh-w4cj-qxq8

# CVE-2026-4372 (transformers RCE — fix: >= 5.3.0)
# CVE-2026-5241 (transformers arbitrary code execution — fix: >= 5.5.0)
#   Package    : transformers < 5.5.0 (transitive via sentence-transformers)
#   Fix        : transformers >= 5.5.0
#   Why blocked: sentence-transformers 3.x (pinned < 4.0.0 in pyproject.toml line 23) is not
#                compatible with transformers 5.x. Forcing transformers >= 5.0.0 would break
#                CrossEncoder and SentenceTransformer model loading.
#                The < 4.0.0 pin is deliberate: sentence-transformers 4.x introduces a mypy
#                CrossEncoder API change that requires a dedicated ML stack migration slice
#                (see TRAIL.md § Deferred Work: "sentence-transformers v4+").
#   Compensating control: model IDs are validated against a fixed allowlist in
#                         server/core/model_registry.py; arbitrary HuggingFace model IDs from
#                         user input are rejected, narrowing the RCE attack surface significantly.
#   Unblocked by: dedicated ML stack upgrade slice (sentence-transformers >= 4.0, transformers >= 5.5).
CVE-2026-4372
CVE-2026-5241

# CVE-2025-32434 (torch arbitrary code execution via torch.load — fix: >= 2.6.0)
#   Package    : torch 2.2.2 (transitive via sentence-transformers)
#   Fix        : torch >= 2.6.0
#   Why blocked: sentence-transformers 3.x (pinned < 4.0.0 in pyproject.toml) pins torch 2.x;
#                upgrading torch to 2.6.0 has not been validated against this project's ST 3.x
#                stack. Additionally, the patched torch wheel is unavailable for macOS x86_64
#                (tracked separately as PYSEC-2026-2286 in pip-audit.sh), which would break
#                local development on that platform.
#   Compensating control: model IDs are validated against a fixed allowlist in
#                         server/core/model_registry.py; torch.load is not called with
#                         attacker-controlled model paths — arbitrary HuggingFace model IDs
#                         from user input are rejected, significantly narrowing the attack surface.
#   Unblocked by: dedicated ML stack upgrade slice (sentence-transformers >= 4.0, torch >= 2.6.0).
CVE-2025-32434
